  "description": "If you’re looking for a rigid adventure bike that you can also chuck around in the woods and isn’t phased by technical singletrack, then our Beyond+ is spot on. Starting with a double butted steel suspension corrected frame with a quad-butted ovalized downtube and matching Seido Steel BPS fork, this is the 4 x 4 of the Beyond line, capable of swallowing huge 27.5 x 2.8’’ WTB Ranger rubber on wide 35 mm rims for that go anywhere experience. Both frame and fork come with multiple mounting points, including offset triple cage mounts on the seat stays and forward-facing mounts on the fork for maximum clearance. Load it up and head off anywhere.\n\n¹ Triple cage mounts on seat stays might fit cargo cages depending on foot position and shoe size. We can't guarantee sufficient clearance for every possible set up and riding style. Those mounts are not only meant for cages, but can also be used for installing pumps, tools, locks or lights.",
